# Felix tracks doctrine and gate. Not memory — see below.
.DS_Store
*.log
# ...except maintenance.log, which felix itself tells you to commit "so the
# cadence survives this machine", and which `*.log` silently untracked. It is
# doctrine: when a routine is due is a rule about the project, not a record of
# a session.
!projects/*/maintenance.log

# Memory left this repository on 2026-08-14 and must never come back. It lives
# under felix_mem_root — outside any checkout — because it holds verbatim
# founder prompts and whatever a governed project's work is about, including
# material belonging to somebody who never agreed to be published.
#
# This rule is the backstop, not the mechanism. The mechanism is that nothing
# writes here any more; the gate's `memory` check fails if anything does. Both
# exist because a gitignore rule alone is one `git add -f` from failing, and
# because a directory that reappears empty is how the old layout would creep
# back one project at a time.
projects/*/memory/

# Never let a project's runtime state or secrets land here.
# `state/` is Felix's own ephemeral scratch: gate receipts and per-session route
# memory. It is rebuilt on demand and must never be committed — and because
# Felix's home is this repository when Felix governs itself, anything written
# there would otherwise change the very tree a receipt is describing.
state/
.claude-flow/
data/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key

# graphify writes its knowledge graph here. It is derived from the tree and
# rebuilt on demand, and an untracked copy in the home invalidates every gate
# receipt: felix_tree_dirty counts untracked files, and the installed check
# reads them as undeployed work.
graphify-out/
